        "image_alt": "Nina Brooks at a long white desk in her studio, lights and a camera around her",
        "eyebrow": "About",
        "heading": "Hi, I'm Nina",
        "text": "<p>For six years I wrote marketing emails for software companies. I liked the writing and disliked everything around it: the meetings, the approvals, the sense that the work belonged to someone else.</p><p>In 2019 I started a small newsletter about what I was learning. A year later I filmed my first video in a spare room, and the year after that I sold a workshop to forty readers. That was the moment it felt like a business.</p><p>Today I make videos, write the Tuesday Letter, host Open Tabs and teach a few courses. Write your own story here.</p>",
